00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:49,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:50,154 --> 00:00:53,324
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

2
00:00:53,407 --> 00:00:55,868
1 YEAR AGO

3
00:01:02,958 --> 00:01:03,959
You can sit.

4
00:01:13,803 --> 00:01:14,887
Did you see the personnel changes?

5
00:01:16,222 --> 00:01:17,473
Yes, I did.

6
00:01:18,099 --> 00:01:19,225
How do you feel about it?

7
00:01:20,601 --> 00:01:21,602
I'm fine with it.

8
00:01:22,144 --> 00:01:23,562
I know that's not true.

9
00:01:25,272 --> 00:01:27,108
No, I really am.

10
00:01:29,151 --> 00:01:31,195
How are you and Eun-tae?
Are you close?

11
00:01:31,570 --> 00:01:33,406
The assistant manager?

12
00:01:33,489 --> 00:01:35,032
Oh, he's team leader now.

13
00:01:36,117 --> 00:01:38,077
Yes, well, we get along fine.

14
00:01:38,911 --> 00:01:41,080
Can you work under him?

15
00:01:42,707 --> 00:01:45,251
Are you sending me to Sales Team 5?

16
00:01:45,334 --> 00:01:46,419
Why?

17
00:01:46,502 --> 00:01:49,213
You don't want to work under
a younger team leader?

18
00:01:51,716 --> 00:01:53,259
It's not just about me.

19
00:01:54,301 --> 00:01:56,554
I think Mr. Gong
might feel uncomfortable.

20
00:01:57,513 --> 00:01:59,098
I'm asking what you think.

21
00:01:59,890 --> 00:02:00,975
You don't want to transfer?

22
00:02:03,978 --> 00:02:05,521
If I have a choice

23
00:02:06,147 --> 00:02:08,816
I'd like to stay where I am.

24
00:02:12,236 --> 00:02:13,237
Hey.

25
00:02:13,696 --> 00:02:14,697
Yes?

26
00:02:15,322 --> 00:02:18,951
I'm telling you to join Team 5
as nicely as I can.

27
00:02:19,493 --> 00:02:21,704
Why do you make me give you an order?

28
00:02:25,791 --> 00:02:27,752
I apologize. I'll transfer.

29
00:02:29,086 --> 00:02:30,463
- You can go.
- Okay.

30
00:02:34,633 --> 00:02:35,718
Ms. Park.

31
00:02:36,802 --> 00:02:39,972
Don't you also think
he and I aren't a good fit?

32
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:43,601
Sorry, ma'am.

33
00:02:47,021 --> 00:02:48,731
I wouldn't send you there
if you two weren't a good fit.

34
00:02:51,025 --> 00:02:53,486
You and Eun-tae might not know it

35
00:02:54,945 --> 00:02:55,988
but you two make a good team.

36
00:03:00,284 --> 00:03:02,828
- Get out.
- Yes, ma'am.

37
00:03:10,503 --> 00:03:13,589
EPISODE 3: WHAT I BELIEVE IN

38
00:03:44,370 --> 00:03:45,579
Aren't you sick of it?

39
00:03:46,789 --> 00:03:47,790
Of what?

40
00:03:47,873 --> 00:03:50,668
Having the same coffee every day
at the same time.

41
00:03:51,544 --> 00:03:55,548
Sometimes, you can have a latte.
Sometimes, you can skip.

42
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:57,424
But you come here without fail.

43
00:03:58,467 --> 00:03:59,468
It's different every day.

44
00:04:01,136 --> 00:04:03,305
I may not be an expert

45
00:04:03,973 --> 00:04:06,225
but the coffee smells different
every day.

46
00:04:07,768 --> 00:04:09,854
That's why I look forward
to each cup.

47
00:04:11,146 --> 00:04:13,357
- I'll see you tomorrow.
- Bye.

48
00:04:21,198 --> 00:04:22,575
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

49
00:04:22,992 --> 00:04:24,118
Morning.

50
00:04:35,796 --> 00:04:37,089
Hello, Mr. Gong.

51
00:04:37,172 --> 00:04:38,382
You're here early, Gi-tae.

52
00:04:38,632 --> 00:04:39,633
Yes.

53
00:04:50,561 --> 00:04:52,104
I'd like to confirm the meeting time.

54
00:04:53,689 --> 00:04:54,815
- Yes.
- Good morning.

55
00:04:58,569 --> 00:04:59,570
Hello.

56
00:05:02,865 --> 00:05:04,575
Great. Thank you.

57
00:05:16,295 --> 00:05:17,713
- Ji-hye.
- Yes?

58
00:05:17,796 --> 00:05:21,884
Can you check the conference room
for our Laknes meeting?

59
00:05:21,967 --> 00:05:23,802
I'd like some extra time
before and after.

60
00:05:23,886 --> 00:05:25,763
The meeting is scheduled
for 2 to 4 p.m.

61
00:05:25,846 --> 00:05:28,474
so I extended the reservation
from 1 to 5 p.m.

62
00:05:28,557 --> 00:05:29,600
Is that okay with you?

63
00:05:30,267 --> 00:05:32,311
- You did that already?
- Yes.

64
00:05:32,394 --> 00:05:35,230
Mr. Yang told me
you'd need some extra time.

65
00:05:42,363 --> 00:05:44,073
- Gi-tae?
- Yes, sir?

66
00:05:44,156 --> 00:05:45,449
Stop what you're doing

67
00:05:45,532 --> 00:05:48,285
and print Alex Cooper's
first-half revenue.

68
00:05:50,412 --> 00:05:51,705
I'm on it right now.

69
00:05:51,789 --> 00:05:53,374
I put him on it already.

70
00:05:54,583 --> 00:05:58,921
And here are the malls and outlets
where our brands are sold.

71
00:05:59,004 --> 00:06:01,173
It should help
with your upcoming meeting.

72
00:06:01,256 --> 00:06:03,300
Thank you, Mr. Yang.

73
00:06:04,385 --> 00:06:05,552
Here you go.

74
00:06:05,928 --> 00:06:07,888
Oh, thanks.

75
00:06:11,976 --> 00:06:13,185
- Ji-hye.
- Yes?

76
00:06:13,268 --> 00:06:16,188
We need two visitor passes
from Support.

77
00:06:16,271 --> 00:06:17,272
Did you...

78
00:06:18,065 --> 00:06:19,108
already get them?

79
00:06:20,234 --> 00:06:21,694
Oh, dear...

80
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:25,447
Ms. Lee, can you get them?

81
00:06:25,531 --> 00:06:28,033
I forgot. I'll get them now.

82
00:06:30,703 --> 00:06:32,413
SUPPLEMENT FOR STOMACH LINING

83
00:06:34,039 --> 00:06:36,041
Mr. Gong, have one of these.

84
00:06:36,125 --> 00:06:37,334
It's good for you.

85
00:06:38,085 --> 00:06:40,421
Thanks. I'll take it later.

86
00:06:40,504 --> 00:06:42,798
No, take it now.

87
00:07:04,737 --> 00:07:06,155
I should've shut him down sooner.

88
00:07:06,238 --> 00:07:08,198
- You liked it?
- Never mind.

89
00:07:12,995 --> 00:07:15,497
They work slower,
so we must be prepared.

90
00:07:18,876 --> 00:07:20,919
- Hello, Mr. Jang.
- Hello.

91
00:07:21,003 --> 00:07:22,004
Hi.

92
00:07:22,171 --> 00:07:23,756
- Oh, I remember.
- Yes.

93
00:07:23,839 --> 00:07:26,258
I'm thinking that's a possibility.

94
00:07:26,717 --> 00:07:29,678
- We should be prepared.
- Sakamoto is...

95
00:07:33,432 --> 00:07:34,433
Hello, sir.

96
00:07:35,684 --> 00:07:36,685
What are you two up to?

97
00:07:38,687 --> 00:07:41,565
We're preparing
for our meeting with Laknes.

98
00:07:42,274 --> 00:07:43,484
- You two?
- Yes.

99
00:07:45,527 --> 00:07:47,821
You... Never mind.

100
00:07:48,822 --> 00:07:51,116
So what's the plan?

101
00:07:52,034 --> 00:07:53,869
Why prepare
when we just need their signature?

102
00:07:53,952 --> 00:07:59,124
We thought we should show them
what we can do.

103
00:07:59,208 --> 00:08:01,668
What we're like when we get to work.

104
00:08:05,964 --> 00:08:09,885
Don't waste your time.
Just get the deal signed.

105
00:08:10,344 --> 00:08:13,138
Oh, and did you sort out
your other brands?

106
00:08:13,722 --> 00:08:16,642
I'm almost done. I'll wrap up soon.

107
00:08:17,101 --> 00:08:19,645
Why are you taking so long?

108
00:08:19,728 --> 00:08:21,438
- Finish up quickly.
- Yes, sir.

109
00:08:26,360 --> 00:08:28,278
- Then...
- Let's continue.

110
00:08:30,656 --> 00:08:34,701
Was Team 4 told to give up
any of your brands?

111
00:08:35,077 --> 00:08:36,787
We're barely surviving as is.
There's nothing to give up.

112
00:08:37,663 --> 00:08:38,664
Why do you ask?

113
00:08:38,956 --> 00:08:43,460
Ms. Joo asked if Team 4 agreed
to hand over any brands.

114
00:08:43,794 --> 00:08:46,046
Does my team need
to give yours anything?

115
00:08:46,797 --> 00:08:51,260
No, I'm just curious
why people are saying that.

116
00:08:52,177 --> 00:08:53,971
- Ju-hui.
- Yes?

117
00:08:54,471 --> 00:08:57,099
Someone from Team 1 or 2
will become associate director, yes?

118
00:08:58,058 --> 00:09:00,144
- Yes.
- Then why is Team 5

119
00:09:00,227 --> 00:09:01,812
giving its brands to Team 1?

120
00:09:04,064 --> 00:09:05,691
Because they have
too much on their plate?

121
00:09:08,026 --> 00:09:10,904
Teams 1 and 2 are competing
to get ahead.

122
00:09:11,446 --> 00:09:13,448
And Team 5 suffers in the process.

123
00:09:14,158 --> 00:09:17,327
It's like two thugs
getting into a bar fight

124
00:09:17,411 --> 00:09:20,164
and a civilian gets hit in the head
by a flying bottle.

125
00:09:20,247 --> 00:09:21,373
Got it?

126
00:09:22,207 --> 00:09:24,334
- Yes.
- You didn't get it.

127
00:09:25,460 --> 00:09:26,670
And Ms. Joo...

128
00:09:27,004 --> 00:09:28,714
She sided with Team 1.

129
00:09:29,173 --> 00:09:30,549
She thinks Mr. Kim will get promoted.

130
00:09:31,008 --> 00:09:32,009
But my team?

131
00:09:32,092 --> 00:09:34,720
No one will get promoted,
and we won't perform that well.

132
00:09:34,803 --> 00:09:36,555
No promotions, no bonuses.

133
00:09:36,930 --> 00:09:41,226
I'm saying,
keep us out of the office politics.

134
00:09:43,437 --> 00:09:45,230
You didn't get that, either.

135
00:09:48,734 --> 00:09:50,068
How did you get in here?

136
00:09:50,986 --> 00:09:51,987
I passed the entrance exam.

137
00:10:00,787 --> 00:10:01,872
Are these urgent?

138
00:10:02,247 --> 00:10:03,248
Somewhat.

139
00:10:06,210 --> 00:10:07,461
When is the Laknes meeting?

140
00:10:09,713 --> 00:10:10,964
It should start soon.

141
00:10:11,381 --> 00:10:12,716
What do you want for the brand?

142
00:10:12,799 --> 00:10:14,968
For us to launch it smoothly.

143
00:10:15,969 --> 00:10:17,763
- That's it?
- Yes.

144
00:10:18,096 --> 00:10:19,389
That's all I want.

145
00:10:20,432 --> 00:10:24,102
Do you think Gong and Yang
can work together after that fight?

146
00:10:25,604 --> 00:10:26,605
They're boys.

147
00:10:26,688 --> 00:10:28,440
They fight, but they make up.

148
00:10:30,651 --> 00:10:35,572
Mr. Jang, whatever the outcome,
this deal will benefit the company.

149
00:10:35,656 --> 00:10:38,992
But I'm not sure
if it'll benefit you too.

150
00:11:08,689 --> 00:11:10,065
- Here you go.
- Thanks.

151
00:11:10,565 --> 00:11:11,608
Everything looks good.

152
00:11:13,068 --> 00:11:14,236
Thank you.

153
00:11:20,534 --> 00:11:22,577
Perfect spacing
between the words and lines.

154
00:11:22,661 --> 00:11:24,288
WELCOME TO HONGSUNG
LAKNES ASIA KIM HYEONG-CHAN, SAKAMOTO

155
00:11:55,986 --> 00:11:57,321
I'm Team Leader Gong Eun-tae.

156
00:11:57,863 --> 00:11:59,823
It's a pleasure to meet you.
I'm Team Leader Gong Eun-tae.

157
00:12:00,949 --> 00:12:02,701
I'm Assistant Manager Yang Jun-ho
from Sales Team 5.

158
00:12:03,201 --> 00:12:05,871
I'm Assistant Manager Yang Jun-ho
from Sales Team 5.

159
00:12:06,496 --> 00:12:09,458
I'm Kim Hyeong-chan,
Director of Asia for Laknes.

160
00:12:10,500 --> 00:12:11,710
Hello, nice to meet you.

161
00:12:11,793 --> 00:12:15,172
I'm Sakamoto.
I oversee the Asian market.

162
00:12:16,006 --> 00:12:17,674
- Shall we?
- Yes.

163
00:12:20,802 --> 00:12:22,596
We have pretty good coffee here.

164
00:12:22,679 --> 00:12:24,473
- I hope you like it.
- Great, thank you.

165
00:12:24,556 --> 00:12:25,807
When did you arrive?

166
00:12:25,891 --> 00:12:27,100
We arrived yesterday.

167
00:12:27,184 --> 00:12:28,685
I see. You flew in yesterday.

168
00:12:28,769 --> 00:12:34,858
If you don't mind, may I tape
the meeting for our records?

169
00:12:36,109 --> 00:12:37,778
- Sure.
- Thank you.

170
00:12:47,037 --> 00:12:51,375
<i>I need you to do something for me</i>
<i>before the Laknes meeting.</i>

171
00:12:52,334 --> 00:12:56,046
<i>Ji-hye, find out what you can</i>
<i>about Kim Hyeong-chan and Sakamoto.</i>

172
00:12:57,005 --> 00:13:00,133
<i>Their past tells you who they are.</i>

173
00:13:03,720 --> 00:13:08,642
I'd like to know how a Korean
became Director of Asia.

174
00:13:08,725 --> 00:13:11,019
As a fellow Korean,
it makes me proud.

175
00:13:11,395 --> 00:13:13,522
I studied fashion design in Spain.

176
00:13:14,147 --> 00:13:17,234
I was lucky enough
to start as a VMD at Zara.

177
00:13:17,609 --> 00:13:21,530
I did that for about three years
before moving to Philipp Plein.

178
00:13:21,613 --> 00:13:25,575
Oh, I think I heard
about a Korean working there.

179
00:13:26,034 --> 00:13:27,828
That's when I met Ms. Park Hyeon-suk.

180
00:13:28,620 --> 00:13:33,708
Then I started my own business,
but it didn't work out.

181
00:13:34,793 --> 00:13:37,963
That's when I joined Laknes.

182
00:13:40,215 --> 00:13:42,717
We could learn a lot from you.

183
00:13:42,801 --> 00:13:45,303
Not at all.
I'm sure you're both very capable.

184
00:13:46,012 --> 00:13:50,308
<i>Gi-tae, list questions we can use</i>
<i>to gain the upper hand.</i>

185
00:13:50,809 --> 00:13:53,270
<i>In negotiations, questions are power.</i>

186
00:13:53,353 --> 00:13:55,981
WOULD YOU CONSIDER HIRING HONGSUNG
STAFF WHEN ESTABLISHING A DESIGN LAB?

187
00:13:56,064 --> 00:13:58,984
Laknes is doing well in Japan, right?

188
00:13:59,067 --> 00:14:04,614
Japan runs its own promotions
to support the brand.

189
00:14:04,698 --> 00:14:08,326
Does the head office provide
a separate promotional budget?

190
00:14:13,748 --> 00:14:17,419
We get 3% of the order value
to spend on promotions.

191
00:14:17,752 --> 00:14:19,296
As much as 3%?

192
00:14:19,754 --> 00:14:21,423
Wow, that's a lot.

193
00:14:21,882 --> 00:14:24,926
What margin did you offer
the Japanese market?

194
00:14:26,344 --> 00:14:29,931
Leather goods at 70%,
and apparel at 75%.

195
00:14:30,557 --> 00:14:35,145
Is it true that you offered us
60% for leather and 65% for apparel?

196
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:39,649
I believe we've settled
the baseline margin.

197
00:14:40,317 --> 00:14:42,569
Isn't there always
room for negotiation?

198
00:14:42,652 --> 00:14:46,406
The truth is,
we were headed for Japan.

199
00:14:46,781 --> 00:14:52,204
We called Ms. Park to say hello,
and she arranged this meeting.

200
00:14:52,621 --> 00:14:55,916
Yes, we know
we requested this meeting.

201
00:14:57,918 --> 00:14:59,044
I'll be honest.

202
00:15:00,420 --> 00:15:03,048
We're especially wary
because Korea failed us once before.

203
00:15:03,673 --> 00:15:06,843
We're already doing just fine
in Japan

204
00:15:07,219 --> 00:15:10,096
so we're not sure
why we should enter Korea again.

205
00:15:12,182 --> 00:15:15,477
<i>I'll go through Laknes's</i>
<i>last five financial statements.</i>

206
00:15:19,189 --> 00:15:21,233
<i>The answer is in the numbers.</i>

207
00:15:23,401 --> 00:15:27,572
The purchasing patterns
and recent changes.

208
00:15:31,868 --> 00:15:34,412
To be frank, we were hesitant too.

209
00:15:35,539 --> 00:15:40,252
We do all the work to improve
brand awareness, and the deal ends.

210
00:15:40,752 --> 00:15:44,839
I know many brands switched partners
for a higher baseline margin.

211
00:15:45,757 --> 00:15:47,175
I'm not saying that's wrong.

212
00:15:47,592 --> 00:15:49,302
I'm saying we take on that risk.

213
00:15:53,848 --> 00:15:58,603
You can give 3% of total sales
as a staff incentive.

214
00:16:01,189 --> 00:16:03,984
That's their livelihood,
so that's a given.

215
00:16:04,526 --> 00:16:06,361
Could you reconsider the margin?

216
00:16:06,444 --> 00:16:09,531
A 65% apparel margin puts you
between Pinster and Mareige.

217
00:16:09,614 --> 00:16:11,783
But Laknes is
nothing like those brands.

218
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:14,744
Are you aware we take back
all the dead stock?

219
00:16:14,828 --> 00:16:16,705
Yes, that's actually
more work for us.

220
00:16:16,997 --> 00:16:19,666
We have to pick up everything
and send it back to France.

221
00:16:19,749 --> 00:16:22,085
The only one who profits
is the logistics company.

222
00:16:22,460 --> 00:16:24,254
How about after the launch

223
00:16:24,713 --> 00:16:27,465
we provide enough product
to stock the outlet stores too?

224
00:16:27,841 --> 00:16:29,134
Would that work?

225
00:16:29,217 --> 00:16:33,346
No, we'll handle the malls
and outlets from the start.

226
00:16:34,139 --> 00:16:37,851
In return, give us the same
70% and 75% margins as Japan.

227
00:16:46,484 --> 00:16:47,485
I'm sorry.

228
00:16:48,361 --> 00:16:49,654
I can't do that.

229
00:17:05,003 --> 00:17:06,671
Hey, how do you think it went?

230
00:17:07,881 --> 00:17:09,758
I think it went badly.

231
00:17:11,551 --> 00:17:12,677
Darn it.

232
00:17:28,568 --> 00:17:30,570
Did you see the look
in Sakamoto's eyes?

233
00:17:30,654 --> 00:17:32,697
- No.
- It was bad.

234
00:17:41,998 --> 00:17:43,375
How did it go, Mr. Gong?

235
00:17:44,167 --> 00:17:46,670
- Mr. Yang?
- Let's go upstairs.

236
00:17:46,753 --> 00:17:48,963
- Okay.
- Be quick.

237
00:17:53,802 --> 00:17:55,595
- Gi-tae.
- Yes?

238
00:17:56,054 --> 00:17:57,263
Do you have plans later?

239
00:17:58,014 --> 00:17:59,015
No.

240
00:17:59,766 --> 00:18:00,767
Ji-hye, you?

241
00:18:01,685 --> 00:18:03,269
I'm free too.

242
00:18:04,187 --> 00:18:05,188
Are you?

243
00:18:05,730 --> 00:18:06,981
Then shall we go out...

244
00:18:08,149 --> 00:18:09,150
No.

245
00:18:09,984 --> 00:18:10,985
- What?
- What?

246
00:18:11,945 --> 00:18:13,571
Forget it. It's no big deal.

247
00:18:16,074 --> 00:18:17,409
Did the deal go okay?

248
00:18:20,286 --> 00:18:22,288
What happened? Yes or no?

249
00:18:24,916 --> 00:18:27,001
Why won't either of you say anything?

250
00:18:29,337 --> 00:18:30,422
Did they sign the deal?

251
00:18:31,464 --> 00:18:32,716
- Mr. Gong.
- What happened?

252
00:18:33,717 --> 00:18:35,051
Let's get a drink later.

253
00:18:37,721 --> 00:18:38,930
Forget the drinks.

254
00:18:40,765 --> 00:18:42,934
- Mr. Yang!
- Mr. Yang? Mr. Gong?

255
00:18:44,728 --> 00:18:47,439
We got 65% for leather,
70% for apparel.

256
00:18:47,689 --> 00:18:51,234
We increased the margins by 5%
with a separate incentive clause.

257
00:18:54,028 --> 00:18:56,114
- Good job.
- Thank you.

258
00:18:56,573 --> 00:18:59,325
I owe it to you
for letting us do our jobs.

259
00:18:59,617 --> 00:19:02,412
Also, Mr. Yang played a huge role.

260
00:19:04,497 --> 00:19:07,167
These are the brands
that grew under our management.

261
00:19:07,584 --> 00:19:10,795
They all grew by over 50%
from the previous year.

262
00:19:18,219 --> 00:19:21,014
We're not asking for a higher margin
without reason.

263
00:19:21,097 --> 00:19:24,642
We're asking you to recognize
the value of our work.

264
00:19:25,643 --> 00:19:29,564
We can deliver better results
than anyone else.

265
00:19:30,356 --> 00:19:34,068
The document you're reading
proves that.

266
00:19:41,367 --> 00:19:45,121
What does the Korean market
mean to Laknes?

267
00:19:47,749 --> 00:19:49,918
It's a stepping stone to China

268
00:19:50,001 --> 00:19:53,087
so you don't lose anything
as long as you make a decent profit.

269
00:19:54,547 --> 00:19:56,758
That's why your brand
ended up with our team.

270
00:19:57,717 --> 00:19:59,552
We're the weakest team.

271
00:20:00,094 --> 00:20:04,098
They expect us to do an average job
and give you what you want.

272
00:20:05,183 --> 00:20:10,313
You two expected to come here,
sign the deal, and move on.

273
00:20:10,396 --> 00:20:11,397
Am I wrong?

274
00:20:14,692 --> 00:20:16,236
No, I won't deny that.

275
00:20:16,528 --> 00:20:18,655
I'm sorry, but we have
no intention of doing that.

276
00:20:19,155 --> 00:20:21,658
To you, Korea might be
just a stepping stone

277
00:20:21,741 --> 00:20:24,744
but to us, Laknes is a brand
we must build and grow.

278
00:20:25,578 --> 00:20:28,206
We don't want to settle
for an average profit.

279
00:20:29,499 --> 00:20:31,167
Adjust the margin.

280
00:20:31,501 --> 00:20:33,002
You'll make much more.

281
00:20:34,754 --> 00:20:36,881
Are you that confident?

282
00:20:39,259 --> 00:20:40,468
You saw the numbers.

283
00:20:47,642 --> 00:20:49,018
Good job.

284
00:20:51,396 --> 00:20:52,605
You deserve a team dinner.

285
00:20:54,482 --> 00:20:55,733
Put it on this card.

286
00:20:56,317 --> 00:20:57,318
Thank you.

287
00:20:58,111 --> 00:20:59,112
Mr. Gong.

288
00:20:59,821 --> 00:21:02,282
Did you consider which brands
to give Team 1?

289
00:21:02,657 --> 00:21:04,367
Yes, I did.

290
00:21:04,826 --> 00:21:05,827
<i>Mr. Yang.</i>

291
00:21:06,661 --> 00:21:08,538
Do you want to shake things up
with me?

292
00:21:10,331 --> 00:21:12,000
You're making me feel uneasy.

293
00:21:13,334 --> 00:21:15,086
I'm going to turn
this company around.

294
00:21:18,840 --> 00:21:20,508
We'll keep them all.

295
00:21:22,760 --> 00:21:25,054
What do you mean
you'll keep them all?

296
00:21:25,597 --> 00:21:26,931
We keep all our brands?

297
00:21:28,516 --> 00:21:30,476
What happens then?

298
00:21:31,519 --> 00:21:32,520
Who knows?

299
00:21:33,646 --> 00:21:35,106
That's why I said, "shake things up."

300
00:21:35,815 --> 00:21:37,108
What are you saying?

301
00:21:37,483 --> 00:21:39,319
- You can't do all...
- Let him talk.

302
00:21:40,278 --> 00:21:41,696
Aren't you being too ambitious?

303
00:21:41,946 --> 00:21:43,156
You lack the manpower.

304
00:21:43,531 --> 00:21:47,327
That's why I'd appreciate it
if you gave us some extra help.

305
00:21:48,036 --> 00:21:49,913
Then can you handle it all?

306
00:21:49,996 --> 00:21:50,997
Yes, we can.

307
00:21:51,456 --> 00:21:53,291
I've already assigned the tasks.

308
00:21:53,541 --> 00:21:55,209
I think it's doable.

309
00:21:57,962 --> 00:21:59,756
<i>Will Mr. Jang be okay with that?</i>

310
00:22:00,006 --> 00:22:02,050
I can see his furious expression.

311
00:22:02,884 --> 00:22:05,511
That's for me to handle
as team leader.

312
00:22:09,557 --> 00:22:12,852
I don't know anything
about office politics.

313
00:22:13,227 --> 00:22:17,523
I just don't want someone else
to benefit from my hard work.

314
00:22:18,858 --> 00:22:20,735
You know nothing
about office politics?

315
00:22:20,818 --> 00:22:23,363
Politics and I don't mix.

316
00:22:27,700 --> 00:22:28,910
Let's do it, then.

317
00:22:31,788 --> 00:22:33,247
Sales Team 2.

318
00:22:34,624 --> 00:22:35,625
Yes.

319
00:22:36,084 --> 00:22:37,085
Mr. Son?

320
00:22:37,919 --> 00:22:39,796
Okay, I'll pass it on.

321
00:22:41,339 --> 00:22:42,382
What is it?

322
00:22:42,465 --> 00:22:45,051
- A team leader meeting.
- Right now?

323
00:22:45,134 --> 00:22:46,135
Okay.

324
00:22:47,053 --> 00:22:48,972
- You have a meeting, Mr. Jeong.
- With whom?

325
00:22:49,055 --> 00:22:51,140
- Ms. Park.
- Darn it.

326
00:22:52,225 --> 00:22:54,852
This is just stupid.

327
00:23:03,611 --> 00:23:05,530
- Mr. Yang.
<i>- Is it done yet?</i>

328
00:23:05,613 --> 00:23:08,491
We're almost done.
How far did you get?

329
00:23:08,574 --> 00:23:10,535
- It's printing now.
- We're printing it now.

330
00:23:10,618 --> 00:23:12,954
<i>- Hurry up.</i>
- We'll be right down.

331
00:23:19,127 --> 00:23:21,379
Ji-hye, mine will be printed first.

332
00:23:29,595 --> 00:23:30,930
Here's what you asked for.

333
00:23:31,014 --> 00:23:32,432
This covers each team's brands

334
00:23:32,515 --> 00:23:34,600
and this includes the sales figures.

335
00:23:34,684 --> 00:23:37,186
This is each team's current schedule.

336
00:23:38,771 --> 00:23:41,482
- Good job, both of you.
- Will they be okay with this?

337
00:23:41,816 --> 00:23:43,901
Mr. Jang looked sour.

338
00:23:44,360 --> 00:23:47,155
There's no going back now.
It can't be helped.

339
00:23:49,907 --> 00:23:51,868
- Good luck, sir.
- Good luck, Mr. Gong.

340
00:23:53,119 --> 00:23:57,582
It's almost time to clock out,
so I'll keep this short.

341
00:23:58,082 --> 00:23:59,083
Okay.

342
00:23:59,917 --> 00:24:03,796
Sales Team 5 took on Laknes,
a brand no one else wanted

343
00:24:03,880 --> 00:24:05,882
and signed the deal in our favor.

344
00:24:07,133 --> 00:24:08,342
Let's give them a hand.

345
00:24:14,057 --> 00:24:19,479
The original plan was for them
to hand a few brands to Team 1.

346
00:24:20,229 --> 00:24:22,148
But Mr. Gong changed his mind.

347
00:24:23,858 --> 00:24:25,443
He'll keep them all.

348
00:24:26,903 --> 00:24:30,531
I called you all here
to praise him publicly.

349
00:24:31,783 --> 00:24:33,826
Mr. Gong, what's your reasoning?

350
00:24:39,916 --> 00:24:42,627
I thought that was why
my team was created.

351
00:24:43,419 --> 00:24:44,962
Sales Team 1 is a core team

352
00:24:45,546 --> 00:24:49,926
that handles 30%
of our division's total sales.

353
00:24:50,343 --> 00:24:52,887
I shouldn't burden them with brands

354
00:24:53,137 --> 00:24:55,348
that are only starting
to turn a profit.

355
00:24:56,891 --> 00:24:58,059
I'd like our team

356
00:24:58,893 --> 00:25:00,353
to handle its own business.

357
00:25:03,815 --> 00:25:06,359
Mr. Son, what do you think?

358
00:25:07,485 --> 00:25:08,736
I respect him.

359
00:25:10,071 --> 00:25:13,741
I didn't think the youngest
team leader had that kind of idea.

360
00:25:14,200 --> 00:25:15,576
- You respect him?
- Yes.

361
00:25:16,077 --> 00:25:17,954
Shouldn't you be ashamed of yourself?

362
00:25:20,998 --> 00:25:23,334
- Mr. Kim.
- Yes, ma'am.

363
00:25:24,043 --> 00:25:25,336
What do you think?

364
00:25:27,755 --> 00:25:28,756
I'm ashamed.

365
00:25:29,549 --> 00:25:31,551
- Are you?
- Yes.

366
00:25:32,510 --> 00:25:34,428
- Ms. Joo.
- Yes, ma'am.

367
00:25:35,429 --> 00:25:38,641
I hear you're still bullying brands
into giving you their new products.

368
00:25:39,058 --> 00:25:40,059
Is that true?

369
00:25:43,312 --> 00:25:44,647
You should know better.

370
00:25:47,275 --> 00:25:49,235
- What about you, Mr. Jeong?
- Yes?

371
00:25:50,027 --> 00:25:52,822
I'm embarrassed as well.

372
00:25:53,865 --> 00:25:56,284
The other team leaders
are competing to get ahead.

373
00:25:56,742 --> 00:26:01,414
Have you decided to do nothing
since you won't get promoted, anyway?

374
00:26:02,999 --> 00:26:04,125
That's not it.

375
00:26:07,253 --> 00:26:08,296
Guys.

376
00:26:08,754 --> 00:26:09,964
- Yes?
- Yes?

377
00:26:11,841 --> 00:26:13,926
No one will say it out loud

378
00:26:14,802 --> 00:26:17,263
but you all know
why Laknes went to Team 5

379
00:26:17,638 --> 00:26:20,224
why Team 5 was supposed
to give its brands to Team 1

380
00:26:20,308 --> 00:26:22,226
and who will be promoted
to associate director.

381
00:26:22,310 --> 00:26:25,229
You're all playing chess
in your heads.

382
00:26:26,689 --> 00:26:29,692
You all think you're so smart.

383
00:26:32,069 --> 00:26:33,070
Mr. Jang.

384
00:26:33,738 --> 00:26:34,739
Yes, ma'am.

385
00:26:35,031 --> 00:26:36,949
Jang Hyang-eun returns from China.

386
00:26:37,283 --> 00:26:38,951
Yes, she'll be back next week.

387
00:26:39,827 --> 00:26:40,912
Send her to Team 5.

388
00:26:43,080 --> 00:26:44,081
Yes, ma'am.

389
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:47,752
Make yourselves useful.

390
00:26:48,753 --> 00:26:50,421
Don't just scheme.

391
00:26:51,088 --> 00:26:52,089
Do some work.

392
00:26:57,553 --> 00:26:58,638
Bye, ma'am.

393
00:27:08,356 --> 00:27:09,649
Everyone leave
except for Gong Eun-tae.

394
00:27:19,659 --> 00:27:21,160
TEAM LEADER GONG EUN-TAE

395
00:27:35,508 --> 00:27:38,010
Mr. Jeong, where's Mr. Gong?

396
00:27:38,094 --> 00:27:41,305
He'll need some time
to clean up the mess he made.

397
00:27:41,389 --> 00:27:42,515
You can go home.

398
00:27:46,310 --> 00:27:47,311
Go home.

399
00:27:57,989 --> 00:27:59,073
Why did you do it?

400
00:28:04,620 --> 00:28:06,122
Why won't you answer me?

401
00:28:08,291 --> 00:28:10,918
Why didn't you do as I said?

402
00:28:14,213 --> 00:28:16,465
I did as you said.

403
00:28:17,967 --> 00:28:19,802
You told me to take on Laknes,
so I did.

404
00:28:20,261 --> 00:28:22,680
And I listed up the brands
to give to Team 1.

405
00:28:23,848 --> 00:28:27,977
But then I thought I could do it all
with one extra teammate.

406
00:28:28,394 --> 00:28:30,646
Can't I at least ask for that?

407
00:28:34,650 --> 00:28:36,485
What's gotten into you?

408
00:28:37,236 --> 00:28:40,281
Why are you talking back
like you have nothing to lose?

409
00:28:41,240 --> 00:28:43,743
You don't know your place
now that you're a team leader?

410
00:28:44,535 --> 00:28:45,536
That's not it.

411
00:28:46,370 --> 00:28:50,166
Now that I'm a team leader,
I know what the job entails.

412
00:28:53,419 --> 00:28:58,382
Gosh, you're talking like
you've lost a few screws.

413
00:28:58,716 --> 00:29:00,509
Okay, then.

414
00:29:02,011 --> 00:29:04,472
Do you think team leaders
have a fixed job description?

415
00:29:04,555 --> 00:29:06,098
Who decided that?

416
00:29:07,725 --> 00:29:08,768
Gong Eun-tae.

417
00:29:09,560 --> 00:29:11,812
Team leaders,
associate directors, and directors...

418
00:29:11,896 --> 00:29:15,649
They're all people
who do as they're told.

419
00:29:16,025 --> 00:29:19,278
If you can't do that,
just start your own business.

420
00:29:20,780 --> 00:29:22,114
This company

421
00:29:22,823 --> 00:29:24,533
isn't yours, is it?

422
00:29:24,825 --> 00:29:25,826
You bastard!

423
00:29:26,369 --> 00:29:28,621
I can't believe what I'm hearing.

424
00:29:28,954 --> 00:29:29,955
Mr. Jang.

425
00:29:31,582 --> 00:29:32,917
In my first year here

426
00:29:33,292 --> 00:29:38,297
do you remember taking clueless me
to Paris to sign a deal?

427
00:29:38,381 --> 00:29:39,840
What about it?

428
00:29:40,341 --> 00:29:42,343
We took a red-eye on Saturday.

429
00:29:43,219 --> 00:29:44,845
We worked all weekend

430
00:29:44,929 --> 00:29:47,014
and went straight to another meeting
when we landed Tuesday.

431
00:29:48,391 --> 00:29:50,309
I did that for just one week

432
00:29:50,935 --> 00:29:55,606
but you'd been doing that
for the whole month.

433
00:29:58,776 --> 00:30:00,069
Sure, we were busy.

434
00:30:00,152 --> 00:30:03,155
We couldn't send anyone else.
So what?

435
00:30:04,865 --> 00:30:06,117
You did that

436
00:30:06,992 --> 00:30:09,328
because, like me now,
you were the youngest team leader.

437
00:30:09,954 --> 00:30:12,206
You worked that hard

438
00:30:12,790 --> 00:30:15,167
because you didn't want
your team to suffer

439
00:30:15,251 --> 00:30:17,211
for having the youngest team leader.

440
00:30:18,129 --> 00:30:19,547
Thanks to your sacrifice

441
00:30:19,630 --> 00:30:21,882
we were able to keep our heads down
and work hard.

442
00:30:25,928 --> 00:30:26,929
Hey.

443
00:30:28,848 --> 00:30:30,808
A company is an organization, okay?

444
00:30:31,642 --> 00:30:35,354
Those above lead and pull
while those below support them.

445
00:30:35,729 --> 00:30:39,108
Laknes was my way of telling you
I'd take you with me.

446
00:30:39,567 --> 00:30:42,736
All you had to do was obey
and support me.

447
00:30:45,281 --> 00:30:46,824
I don't know that much yet.

448
00:30:46,907 --> 00:30:49,076
Maybe I'll understand
when I'm an associate director.

449
00:30:50,953 --> 00:30:52,955
You moron...

450
00:30:55,249 --> 00:30:57,001
Mr. Jang.

451
00:30:58,169 --> 00:30:59,753
Back in the day

452
00:31:00,463 --> 00:31:02,423
you argued with staff
at each brand's head office

453
00:31:03,591 --> 00:31:05,301
and sucked up to store staff.

454
00:31:06,385 --> 00:31:10,222
Despite all that,
you bought us soju to cheer us up.

455
00:31:11,724 --> 00:31:15,644
That's how great
a team leader you were.

456
00:31:18,397 --> 00:31:22,651
Can't I be a team leader like you?

457
00:31:27,781 --> 00:31:29,575
Did you get a job offer?

458
00:31:31,202 --> 00:31:33,579
You can be honest.

459
00:31:34,288 --> 00:31:35,289
You did.

460
00:31:35,372 --> 00:31:39,293
Either that, or you're doing this
because you have a Plan B.

461
00:31:40,002 --> 00:31:41,962
No? What is it, then?

462
00:31:42,630 --> 00:31:44,089
Did you win the lottery or something?

463
00:31:46,842 --> 00:31:47,968
Darn it.

464
00:32:05,361 --> 00:32:06,529
I got scared as hell.

465
00:32:23,837 --> 00:32:25,297
You sly thing.

466
00:32:29,510 --> 00:32:31,220
I can't stand you.

467
00:32:33,430 --> 00:32:36,475
- They should be done by now.
- Right?

468
00:32:37,184 --> 00:32:38,227
Hey, look.

469
00:32:44,775 --> 00:32:45,985
You didn't go home?

470
00:32:46,527 --> 00:32:47,945
Well...

471
00:32:49,530 --> 00:32:51,574
Were you afraid
I'd kill your team leader?

472
00:32:51,657 --> 00:32:53,534
Gosh, no.

473
00:32:54,201 --> 00:32:55,536
We're going out to dinner.

474
00:33:01,625 --> 00:33:03,961
You're a weird bunch.

475
00:33:04,795 --> 00:33:07,631
Just a few days ago,
you wanted to tear each other apart.

476
00:33:09,049 --> 00:33:10,843
- Here.
- No, thanks.

477
00:33:10,926 --> 00:33:12,469
Ms. Park gave me hers.

478
00:33:12,803 --> 00:33:14,179
I'll pay for the second round.

479
00:33:15,139 --> 00:33:16,807
Okay, then. Thank you.

480
00:33:18,475 --> 00:33:19,893
- Mr. Yang.
- Yes, sir.

481
00:33:20,769 --> 00:33:23,939
Your team leader loves beef so much
it'll wake him right up.

482
00:33:24,398 --> 00:33:26,191
- Have beef for dinner.
- Okay.

483
00:33:26,442 --> 00:33:28,152
- And go somewhere cheap for round 2.
- Got it.

484
00:33:29,361 --> 00:33:30,487
- Thank you.
- Bye, sir.

485
00:33:30,571 --> 00:33:31,697
Thank you.

486
00:33:38,662 --> 00:33:39,788
Hey, Eun-tae.

487
00:33:41,248 --> 00:33:42,499
Laknes...

488
00:33:43,375 --> 00:33:44,418
It'll do well.

489
00:33:45,252 --> 00:33:47,171
I wouldn't have given it to you
otherwise.

490
00:33:57,264 --> 00:33:58,307
Let's go.

491
00:33:58,724 --> 00:34:00,142
- Yes, sir.
- Okay.

492
00:34:28,045 --> 00:34:29,421
Do you know what to do?

493
00:34:36,095 --> 00:34:37,554
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

494
00:34:41,558 --> 00:34:43,143
Snap, snap.

495
00:35:07,251 --> 00:35:08,502
<i>You're embarrassed?</i>

496
00:35:09,503 --> 00:35:12,005
The other team leaders
are competing to get ahead.

497
00:35:12,506 --> 00:35:17,344
<i>Have you decided to do nothing</i>
<i>since you won't get promoted, anyway?</i>

498
00:35:25,477 --> 00:35:26,562
Good job, everyone.

499
00:35:26,645 --> 00:35:28,397
- You too.
- Good work.

500
00:35:32,276 --> 00:35:35,738
Mr. Gong, I feel awesome today.

501
00:35:36,488 --> 00:35:37,656
Why is that?

502
00:35:38,198 --> 00:35:39,408
It's like...

503
00:35:39,992 --> 00:35:43,829
I feel like I helped close this deal.

504
00:35:43,912 --> 00:35:45,122
That's why I feel good.

505
00:35:45,414 --> 00:35:48,917
I didn't actually do anything,
but that's how I feel.

506
00:35:49,001 --> 00:35:51,795
You're right. You didn't do anything.

507
00:35:52,087 --> 00:35:54,506
- What?
- We all did it together.

508
00:35:54,590 --> 00:35:56,300
Right, Mr. Gong?

509
00:35:56,383 --> 00:35:58,427
- See?
- Okay, let's go with that.

510
00:35:58,510 --> 00:35:59,595
"Let's go with that"?

511
00:36:01,346 --> 00:36:04,683
I appreciate Mr. Jang more now.

512
00:36:05,809 --> 00:36:06,852
How so?

513
00:36:07,478 --> 00:36:09,897
He said you liked beef

514
00:36:09,980 --> 00:36:11,774
and he gave us his corporate card.

515
00:36:12,191 --> 00:36:14,485
He also said Laknes would do well.

516
00:36:16,320 --> 00:36:17,654
He's like that.

517
00:36:18,071 --> 00:36:21,658
He knows exactly when to use
the carrot and the stick.

518
00:36:21,742 --> 00:36:24,203
It all worked out today, though.

519
00:36:24,286 --> 00:36:27,331
That's why I don't resent Mr. Jang

520
00:36:28,207 --> 00:36:29,750
even when he yells and curses me out.

521
00:36:29,833 --> 00:36:31,710
His praise means
just as little to me.

522
00:36:32,628 --> 00:36:36,548
I don't trust others enough
to let their words sway me.

523
00:36:39,301 --> 00:36:42,137
What do you believe in, then?

524
00:37:08,330 --> 00:37:09,373
<i>My past.</i>

525
00:37:15,462 --> 00:37:17,422
I believe in the life I've lived.

526
00:37:22,678 --> 00:37:24,638
That's so freaking cool.

527
00:37:25,222 --> 00:37:27,266
Can I quote that?

528
00:37:27,349 --> 00:37:28,934
No, don't you dare.

529
00:37:29,893 --> 00:37:32,521
"My past. I believe in the life..."

530
00:37:34,022 --> 00:37:36,191
Don't imitate me. It's embarrassing.

531
00:37:36,275 --> 00:37:37,442
Did I say it wrong?

532
00:37:37,526 --> 00:37:39,611
You shouldn't put so much faith
in your past.

533
00:37:39,695 --> 00:37:41,321
- That'll end badly.
- Why?

534
00:37:41,405 --> 00:37:42,739
- Can I try?
- Sure.

535
00:37:42,823 --> 00:37:45,742
"My past.
I believe in the life I've lived."

536
00:37:45,826 --> 00:37:47,452
- I said it better.
- Excuse me.

537
00:37:47,536 --> 00:37:49,746
You can't say it better than me.

538
00:37:49,830 --> 00:37:51,456
Say it properly, will you?

539
00:37:51,540 --> 00:37:53,166
"My past. I believe in my past."

540
00:37:53,250 --> 00:37:55,127
- Is that not right?
- You said it wrong.

541
00:37:55,752 --> 00:37:57,129
Why are you calling so late?

542
00:37:57,212 --> 00:37:59,298
The time is the least of our worries.

543
00:37:59,381 --> 00:38:01,675
The girl returning from China
is joining your team?

544
00:38:02,593 --> 00:38:03,594
Jang Hyang-eun.

545
00:38:03,927 --> 00:38:06,013
Jang Hyang-eun returns from China.

546
00:38:06,096 --> 00:38:07,806
Yes, she'll be back next week.

547
00:38:09,141 --> 00:38:10,350
Send her to Team 5.

548
00:38:11,143 --> 00:38:13,562
<i>Yes, she'll join my team. Why?</i>

549
00:38:13,937 --> 00:38:15,856
<i>You accepted her willingly?</i>

550
00:38:15,939 --> 00:38:18,525
<i>I did. She's good at her job.</i>

551
00:38:20,235 --> 00:38:24,031
Gong, I didn't mention this
because it's classified.

552
00:38:24,656 --> 00:38:26,658
The China branch is about to implode.

553
00:38:30,329 --> 00:38:31,413
What do you mean?

554
00:38:32,164 --> 00:38:34,541
<i>The branch was deeply corrupt.</i>

555
00:38:35,125 --> 00:38:39,129
<i>Word is, Jang Hyang-eun</i>
<i>was at the center of it all.</i>

556
00:38:40,130 --> 00:38:41,924
I think you picked the wrong person.

557
00:39:17,960 --> 00:39:22,881
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

558
00:39:35,268 --> 00:39:38,230
That's why your brand
ended up with our team.

559
00:39:38,689 --> 00:39:41,274
We're the weakest team.

560
00:39:42,275 --> 00:39:47,197
They expect us to do an average job
and give you what you want.

561
00:39:48,699 --> 00:39:55,664
You two expected to come here,
sign the deal, and move on.

562
00:39:56,999 --> 00:39:58,083
Am I wrong?

563
00:40:00,794 --> 00:40:02,295
Okay, next.

564
00:40:03,380 --> 00:40:05,924
<i>I'm sorry, but we have</i>
<i>no intention of doing that.</i>

565
00:40:06,008 --> 00:40:08,093
"I'm sorry, but we have..."

566
00:40:08,385 --> 00:40:11,388
<i>To you, Korea might be</i>
<i>just a stepping stone</i>

567
00:40:11,471 --> 00:40:14,683
<i>but to us, Laknes is a brand</i>
<i>we must build and grow.</i>

568
00:40:15,392 --> 00:40:17,227
<i>Adjust the margin.</i>

569
00:40:17,728 --> 00:40:19,354
<i>You'll make that much more.</i>

570
00:40:20,480 --> 00:40:22,232
<i>Are you that confident?</i>

571
00:40:23,233 --> 00:40:24,526
<i>You saw the numbers.</i>

572
00:40:27,029 --> 00:40:29,322
"You saw the numbers."

573
00:40:34,703 --> 00:40:35,954
You saw the numbers.

574
00:40:36,997 --> 00:40:38,457
That's not it.

575
00:40:39,499 --> 00:40:40,500
You saw the numbers.

576
00:40:40,584 --> 00:40:41,835
The numbers. You saw them.

577
00:40:41,918 --> 00:40:43,920
Hey, did you see this? The numbers.

578
00:40:44,004 --> 00:40:45,547
You saw the numbers, didn't you?

579
00:40:46,631 --> 00:40:47,799
You saw the num...

580
00:40:50,677 --> 00:40:52,012
Mr. Gong.

581
00:40:52,596 --> 00:40:53,638
Mr. Yang.

582
00:40:54,222 --> 00:40:55,223
Ji-hye?

583
00:41:07,319 --> 00:41:08,779
What the...

584
00:41:10,530 --> 00:41:12,157
That was so embarrassing.

585
00:43:42,515 --> 00:43:44,517
Subtitles by Jennifer Jean Lim

